## Vendored third-party code

### tomlkit 0.13.3 — MIT

Vendored from its published PyPI wheel into `Source/vendor/tomlkit/` so that
round-trip edits to a user's TOML configuration preserve formatting and
comments.

- Upstream: https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit
- License: MIT — full text at `Source/vendor/tomlkit-LICENSE`
- Wheel SHA-256: `c89c649d79ee40629a9fda55f8ace8c6a1b42deb912b2a8fd8d942ddadb606b0`

`Source/codex_profile.py` inserts `Source/vendor` at the front of `sys.path`,
so the vendored copy is always the one that loads.

## Python dependencies

| Package | Status | License | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `cryptography` 50.0.0 | required | Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause | Fernet sealing of stored reasoning envelopes (`Source/responses_bridge.py`) |
| `tomlkit` 0.13.3 | vendored | MIT | Comment-preserving TOML edits (`Source/codex_profile.py`) |
| `python-dotenv` | optional | BSD-3-Clause | Reading a Vibe-supplied `.env`; a built-in parser is used when absent |
| `certifi` | optional | MPL-2.0 | CA bundle for outbound TLS; falls back to the system trust store |

The two optional packages are imported inside `try`/`except ImportError`
blocks and degrade gracefully. Provider Hub runs without them.

`Source/requirements.txt` is the canonical runtime dependency list and is the
file named in the error shown when `cryptography` is missing from a runtime.
`pyproject.toml` mirrors it for development and CI.

## Chat fonts

Inter (The Inter Project Authors), Source Serif 4 (The Source Serif 4 Project
Authors / Adobe), and JetBrains Mono (The JetBrains Mono Project Authors) are
bundled unmodified under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each font's copyright
notice and complete OFL text accompany it in `Source/fonts/` and the packaged
`Contents/Resources/worker/fonts/` directory. Sources and checksums are recorded
in `Source/fonts/manifest.json`. These font files are not relicensed under the
project's Apache-2.0 licence. Custom fonts are loaded from the user's macOS font
library and are never copied into the distribution.

## Provider logos

The images in `Source/provider-logos/` are third-party brand assets. Their
exact provenance — which came from TaskWraith and which from Limit Counter —
is recorded in `Source/provider-logos/README.md`. That file is the
authoritative attribution and ships alongside the assets.

Those images are **not** covered by the Apache-2.0 grant over the rest of this
repository. Copyright in each logo remains with the respective provider, and
they are reproduced here solely to identify which provider a route connects to.

If you redistribute this project you are responsible for complying with each
mark owner's brand guidelines, and for removing the assets if you cannot. Logo
paths are keyed by provider slug in `Source/provider_branding.json`, so removal
is a contained change.

### Per-mark rights notes

TaskWraith records a rights note for each asset it publishes, in
`design-assets/provider-logos/provider-logos.manifest.json`. The marks this
project ships, and the conditions that came with them:

| Mark | Owner | Condition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Gemini | Google LLC | Official Google Image Library asset; publication use offered **with credit "Source: Google"**. |
| AntiGravity | Google LLC | Icon from the official Google Antigravity press page; preserve unmodified. |
| Codex | OpenAI | Product PNG from OpenAI's developer domain; not part of a public logo pack, and **source availability does not grant redistribution**. |
| Claude | Anthropic PBC | Official media-resource asset; no separate public logo licence found. Retain unmodified, nominative reference only. |
| Kimi | Moonshot AI | First-party guide states all rights reserved. Unmodified, nominative use only; clearance contact `team@moonshot.ai`. |
| Grok | X.AI LLC | Accurate reference permitted subject to brand terms; logos must remain exactly as provided. **Permission is conditional and revocable.** |
| Ollama | Ollama | Sourced from an MIT-licensed repository, but Ollama's terms separately reserve branding rights. Factual identification only. |
| Mistral | Mistral AI | First-party brand page welcomes responsible use; prohibits modification or framing. |
| Muse / Meta | Meta Platforms, Inc. | Locally supplied asset preserved byte-for-byte for identification. |
| Devin | Cognition AI, Inc. | Cognition's brand download links returned 404, so this is the favicon its own documentation site serves. |
| Cerebras | Cerebras Systems, Inc. | Official press-kit PNGs; **Cerebras' terms and any required owner permission govern external or public reuse.** |
| DeepSeek | Hangzhou DeepSeek AI Co., Ltd. | Official repository publishes the source SVG; the PNG is a derivative recorded upstream as **design reference only**. DeepSeek's User Agreement restricts independent logo use — **do not redistribute without owner permission.** |
| Qwen, OpenRouter | Alibaba, OpenRouter | Sourced via Limit Counter; **no upstream rights note exists for these two.** Clearance status unverified. |

Every mark above ships as the unmodified source asset, with one exception worth
stating plainly: **Devin** is declared `template: true` in
`Source/provider_branding.json`, so `ProviderMark` renders it through SwiftUI
template rendering and paints it in the interface's primary colour rather than
reproducing its own colours. That is a modification of the mark's appearance,
not a byte-for-byte reproduction, and it raises the bar above purely
nominative use. It is disclosed here rather than left implicit.

Two of these are unresolved for public redistribution and are flagged rather
than papered over: **DeepSeek**, whose upstream note expressly warns against
publishing the PNG derivative, and **Qwen / OpenRouter**, which have no recorded
rights note at all. Shipping them is a deliberate decision by the copyright
holder, not an oversight.

